package protocol

const BrowserExistingTargetInstructions = " For work in an already signed-in browser, discover permitted profiles and extension versions, then browser_open(mode=personal,reuse_only=true,exact_url=...,profile_id/window_id when known). Never fall back to clean/persistent or navigate an unrelated tab to satisfy an existing-session task. Inspect binding_verified, readable, actual URL/title/window and page preview. auth_state=unverified requires confirming the visible account/content; session ready alone proves no login. Reuse binding_revision with every subsequent call to that target. Rebind on binding_changed, tab_not_found or stale connection; do not silently switch profile/window. Use scoped/light snapshots and message IDs for virtualized lists; a truncated snapshot or unchanged viewport does not prove end of history. Preserve original download bytes; neither small file size nor image dimensions proves preview/original quality. Signed URLs, cookies and tokens must not be copied into logs or manifests. Verify one complete capture before a batch, persist checkpoints by stable message/attachment IDs, rebuild counts from completed files, and report partial coverage honestly."
